  "notes": "USAGE:\nPrimarily used for catching wild animals, especially in news reports about pest control, wildlife management, or escaped animals. Less commonly used for capturing enemy combatants or vessels. More formal than {捕|つか}まえる (to catch).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {捕獲|ほかく}する: to capture\n- {捕獲|ほかく}される: to be captured\n- {生|い}け{捕獲|ほかく}: capture alive\n- {捕獲|ほかく}{作戦|さくせん}: capture operation\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {捕|つか}まえる: to catch (everyday, general)\n- {逮捕|たいほ}: arrest (for people, legal context)\n- {拿捕|だほ}: seizure (of ships)",
